dmissions Financial Aid Rabb School of Continuing Studies Research Centers and Institutes Funding Resources Athletics Student Life Housing/Community Living Dining Clubs and Organizations Community Service Athletics Arts Rose Art Museum About Our Story Our Jewish Roots Mission and Diversity Statements Fast Facts Visiting Administration Visit Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Giving Popular Resources Campus Calendar Directories Employment Moodle News/Media Orientation Shuttle Schedules Support at Brandeis Workday Sites A-Z Office of Human Resources Home / Careers at Brandeis / Staff Positions Staff Positions External Applicants for Staff Positions New Applicants Applicants applying for the first time must create a new user account and profile on Workday . You may upload and save your resumé to apply for future positions, or create your resumé directly on the system. Returning Applicants Login to your Workday user profile to search and apply for career opportunities, review your application history, edit existing application(s) and upload a new resumé or edit your user profile. Internal Applicants for Staff Positions Current Brandeis employees should search for new opportunities via Workday . To search for open positions, login to Workday, click on the \"Careers\" icon and then click the \"Find Jobs\" tab. To apply for a position, click on the position title link and then click the orange \"Apply\" icon at the top of the page. You may upload your resumé and cover letter as a single document. Brandeis University recognizes the importance of staff development and supports the ability for current employees to apply for internal opportunities of interest that will enhance the employee's skills. An employee must have completed twelve months of employment in good standing in their current role in order to be eligible for an internal transfer or promotion. The waiting period may be waived in cases of a position elimination or other adverse changes to their current position. For additional information, review the Staff Transfers and Promotions policy. Internal applicants will be expected to complete the screening process along with any other candidates. Students and temporary employees should apply as an external applicant. 2026 Presidential Search Careers at Brandeis Faculty Positions Staff Positions Executive Positions Compensation Employee Benefits Employee Support and Well-Being Professional Development Policies, Forms, and Procedures Calendar of Events Meet the Teams Contact Us Home Campus Map and Directions Find University Policies and Procedures Forms Human Resources Staff Workday at Brandeis Explore Careers at Brandeis Employee Benefits Professional Development Calendar of Events Contact Us Office of Human Resources Bernstein-Marcus, 2nd Floor MS 118 Brandeis University 415 South Street Waltham, MA 02453 781-736-4474 humanresources@brandeis.edu Follow Brandeis Brandeis University ©2026 All rights reserved. University Policies Accessibility Statement Privacy Emergency Services"
